==County coding==
From 1939 through 1965 and from 1971 through 1988, Tennessee license plates began with a one- or two-digit county code. The order of the codes was based on the respective populations of each county.

The codes remained constant from 1939 through 1965, then were re-allocated according to population shifts in 1971, 1976 and 1983.<ref>{{cite web |last=Nicholson |first=David |title=Tennessee County Codes |url=http://www.15q.net/tnco.html |publisher=15q.net |access-date=June 1, 2015}}</ref>

